X-Deja-AN: 493599458
Organization: Hewlett-Packard Consulting
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.misc

I am having an intermitant failure with an RPC in the server that I am
working with.  The "signature" of the failure is quite peculiar!  I
have verified that the same input to this given RPC (I verified all
[in] params) will work sometimes and fail sometimes.  Furthermore, the
same input always causes the same output (I verified the values of all
[out] paramters) as one would typically hope - even in the case of the
failure.

From the above, I have deduced that this is probably not a data
problem in the RPC implementation itself.  I have enable i2dl tracing
for this server and have found that the failure occurs following the
successful completion of the manager (RPC) code and transmission
section of the server stub code on the way back to the client.  I have
my i2dl trace string set up to trace the maximum for all levels.  No
errors appear in this or other standard DCE log files.  

The end symtom is that my server dumps core (usually with a
SIGBUS) and the client gets an RPC failure return code.  The stack
trace always seems to indicate rpc_ss_free and its descendants which
appear to be called by the server stub (as my manager code has already
exited successfully).

I'd welcome any thoughts on how to proceeed from here or ideas on what
the source of the trouble mught be.

Thanks in advance,

Todd Gould
